Subject: [PATCH] DisplayMetrics: the emulator density property is read only on an emulator

getDeviceDensity() read qemu.sf.lcd_density (the density override of the Android emulator) before
ro.sf.lcd_density, in every app. Reading it maps the property area of its context
(qemu_sf_lcd_density_prop) into the app, and root / integrity checkers (Duck Detector) report that
mapping as a virtual machine. It is now read only when ro.boot.qemu says the system runs in the
emulator; on the console the density is ro.sf.lcd_density, as before.

--- a/core/java/android/util/DisplayMetrics.java
+++ b/core/java/android/util/DisplayMetrics.java
@@ -506,11 +506,17 @@
     }
 
     private static int getDeviceDensity() {
+        final int density = SystemProperties.getInt("ro.sf.lcd_density", DENSITY_DEFAULT);
         // qemu.sf.lcd_density can be used to override ro.sf.lcd_density
         // when running in the emulator, allowing for dynamic configurations.
         // The reason for this is that ro.sf.lcd_density is write-once and is
         // set by the init process when it parses build.prop before anything else.
-        return SystemProperties.getInt("qemu.sf.lcd_density",
-                SystemProperties.getInt("ro.sf.lcd_density", DENSITY_DEFAULT));
+        // PocketDS: read only on an emulator. Reading it maps the property area of the emulator
+        // (qemu_sf_lcd_density_prop) into every app, which root and integrity checkers report as
+        // a virtual machine.
+        if (!SystemProperties.getBoolean("ro.boot.qemu", false)) {
+            return density;
+        }
+        return SystemProperties.getInt("qemu.sf.lcd_density", density);
     }
 }
